  "question": {
    "text": "Three separate samples of a solution of a single salt gave these results. One formed a white precipitate with excess ammonia solution, one formed a white precipitate with dil. HCl solution and one formed a black precipitate with $\\mathrm{H}_{2} \\mathrm{~S}$. The salt could be"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "$\\mathrm{AgNO}_{3}$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$\\mathrm{Pb}\\left(\\mathrm{NO}_{3}\\right)_{2}$",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "$\\mathrm{Hg}\\left(\\mathrm{NO}_{3}\\right)_{2}$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$\\mathrm{MnSO}_{4}$",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "B"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\mathrm{Pb}\\left(\\mathrm{NO}_{3}\\right)_{2}+2 \\mathrm{NH}_{4} \\mathrm{OH}$\n$$\n\\begin{array}{r}\n\\rightarrow \\mathrm{Pb}(\\mathrm{OH})_{2} \\downarrow+2 \\mathrm{NH}_{4} \\mathrm{NO}_{3}(\\text { white ppt }) \\\\\n\\mathrm{Pb}\\left(\\mathrm{NO}_{3}\\right)_{2}+2 \\mathrm{HCl} \\rightarrow \\mathrm{PbCl}_{2} \\downarrow+2 \\mathrm{HNO}_{3}(\\text { whiteppt }) \\\\\n\\mathrm{Pb}\\left(\\mathrm{NO}_{3}\\right)_{2}+\\mathrm{H}_{2} \\mathrm{~S} \\rightarrow \\mathrm{PbS} \\downarrow+2 \\mathrm{HNO}_{3} \\text { (black) }\n\\end{array}\n$$"
